{"titulo": "Why Coffee Makes You RUN to the Bathroom 🚽😳", "texto_pantalla": "RUN TO THE BATHROOM", "lote": "C2026112501", "marca": "COFFEE, BUT WHY?", "cuerpo": "pro", "pausa_larga_antes": [1, 6, 7, 13], "nota_datos": "Brown, Cann y Read (1990), Gut 31(4): 29% de 92 encuestados sienten ganas de defecar con café (53% mujeres, 19% hombres); en 8 'respondedores' el colon se activó a los 4 min con café y con descafeinado, duró ≥30 min; agua caliente no produjo aumento. Rao (1998): café 23% más que descafeinado y 60% más que agua. Café y descafeinado estimulan gastrina (McGill OSS). Guion aprobado por Tao 25-nov (línea base). Proporciones del gráfico de agua caliente: ilustrativas (sin aumento).", "frases": ["If coffee sends you running to the bathroom, it's not just the caffeine. And there's a detail almost nobody knows.", "It usually hits in the morning, right after that first cup.", "In 1990, researchers in the UK tested it.", "They placed pressure sensors in volunteers' lower gut, and gave them a cup of coffee.", "In people who felt the urge, the gut started moving within four minutes. And it kept going for at least half an hour.", "They also tested it with plain hot water and no coffee, to compare results. Surprisingly, nothing happened. So it wasn't about a warm drink.", "But here's the detail almost nobody knows, and it changes who this happens to.", "Decaf did it too. Less than regular coffee, but still more than water.", "That's because coffee triggers a gut hormone called gastrin, even without caffeine.", "Gastrin tells your gut to get moving. It's the same kind of signal your body sends after you eat.", "And it doesn't happen to everyone. Only about 3 in 10 people feel it, and women far more than men.", "So if it happens to you, it's your gut waking up.", "Tell me if coffee does this to you.", "Follow for one coffee curiosity a day."], "frases_voz": ["If coffee sends you running to the bathroom, it's not just the caffeine. And there's a detail almost nobody knows.", "It usually hits in the morning, right after that first cup.", "In nineteen ninety, researchers in the UK tested it.", "They placed pressure sensors in volunteers' lower gut, and gave them a cup of coffee.", "In people who felt the urge, the gut started moving within four minutes. And it kept going for at least half an hour.", "They also tested it with plain hot water and no coffee, to compare results. Surprisingly, nothing happened. So it wasn't about a warm drink.", "But here's the detail almost nobody knows, and it changes who this happens to.", "Decaf did it too. Less than regular coffee, but still more than water.", "That's because coffee triggers a gut hormone called gastrin, even without caffeine.", "Gastrin tells your gut to get moving. It's the same kind of signal your body sends after you eat.", "And it doesn't happen to everyone. Only about three in ten people feel it, and women far more than men.", "So if it happens to you, it's your gut waking up.", "Tell me if coffee does this to you.", "Follow for one coffee curiosity a day."], "fuentes": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1378422", "https://www.mcgill.ca/oss/article/health-nutrition/why-does-coffee-make-you-poop", "https://www.healthline.com/health/is-coffee-a-laxative"], "escena": {"momentos": [["s_1", 1, null], ["s_2", 2, null], ["s_3", 3, null], ["s_4", 4, null], ["s_5", 5, null], ["s_6", 6, null], ["s_7", 7, null], ["s_8", 8, null], ["s_9", 9, null], ["s_10", 10, null], ["s_11", 11, null], ["s_fin", 12, null], ["s_cta", 13, null], ["running", 0, "^running"], ["caffeine0", 0, "^caffeine"], ["morning", 1, "^morning"], ["uk", 2, "^uk"], ["sensors", 3, "^sensors"], ["four", 4, "^four"], ["half", 4, "^half"], ["water", 5, "^water"], ["nothing", 5, "^nothing"], ["detail", 6, "^detail"], ["decaf", 7, "^decaf"], ["gastrin", 8, "^gastrin"], ["eat", 9, "^eat"], ["women", 10, "^women"], ["waking", 11, "^waking"]], "escenas": [{"tipo": "pelicula", "desde": "0", "escala": 1.24, "zonas": [{"x0":